{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/325166-stats-for-angels","id":325166,"title":"Stats for Angels","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-29T02:51:22-08:00","id":325166,"title":"Stats for Angels","content":"Were can I find Stats for Angels","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T03:06:28-08:00","id":325187,"title":"","content":"Also can angels be killed ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T03:26:58-08:00","id":325189,"title":"","content":"There are some sample angels in the GMC book, and guidelines for how to build your own depending on Rank.<br /> <br /> As to your second point, yes, they can... theoretically. They tend to be immensely powerful beings, but they also tend to be immensely specialised. So, yes, but doing so is not casual or remotely easy, even assuming that you can identify them as angels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T03:46:43-08:00","id":325197,"title":"","content":"Rules for Angels can be found in the Ephemeral Entities chapter in the God Machine Chronicle or the first appendix of the Demon: the Descent core book. There are some example angels in the Demon: the Descent book starting on page 218 ( near the beginning of the Antagonists chapter/). Angels vary in power considerably.<br /> <br /> IIRC, Angels can be killed, but it's difficult. For it to stick, the Angel would have to be out of Essence when it &quot;died&quot;, otherwise its spirit, for lack of a better term, would be able to reform eventually. The most common way for a mundane character to do this would be to use the Angel's bane against them. Demons could probably do it using the Hellfire Exploit or the Essence Drain demonic Form power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T04:16:03-08:00","id":325204,"title":"","content":"Is there some dice rolls characters can make to help lower the cost on a Pact ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T04:23:56-08:00","id":325207,"title":"","content":"No, that's set by the comparative balance of each side and cannot be altered","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T09:08:25-08:00","id":325316,"title":"","content":"There isn't a roll that lowers the cost of a Pact, but there is a merit in Flowers of Hell called Efficient Dealer that essentially lowers the cost of Pacts that favor the Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T11:54:29-08:00","id":325460,"title":"","content":"In Pacts what can a Demon Deal for ?<br /> Example can A Demon Make a Deal for a Humans Skill at something ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T12:07:44-08:00","id":325467,"title":"","content":"<b>Mortals</b> can get: Merits and Skills. With merits, Mortals can get 1-2 dot merits, adding +1 to their side of the equation, and so on. With skills, Mortals can get +1 to +3 dice bonuses to skills (not actual skill dots), as well as specialties, adding that value to their side of the pact.<br /> <br /> <b>Demons </b>can get: Cover, Cults, and Souls. Demons can get 1, 2, or 3 Cover XP, adding to their side of the pact. The Soul Pact adds 3 points to the Demon's side.<br /> <br /> If the Demon's value is higher than the mortal's value, the Demon has to spend Willpower equal to the difference, in addition to the 1 point to make it work. If the Mortal's value is higher, I don't know. The designers didn't think about what might happen if you want to actually be nice when making a pact &gt;_&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T12:41:26-08:00","id":325485,"title":"","content":"One of my players want to make a deal with some one who plays music but the person wants to quit can the demon make a deal to get that music part of a persons life and then some how when using that part of a cover tap into tht musical talent &gt;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T13:00:49-08:00","id":325507,"title":"","content":"Technically, not by the rules, which is good, otherwise Demons could just circumvent the entire beats/XP system with one mortal intermediary (give mortal skills, have other demon take skills, give mortal skills, have other demon take skills, mostly for free as long as the Willpower is flowing) - however, nothing stops you from using the Cover XP to buy up that cover, then use it to generate Legend.<br /> <br /> There's also no reason you can't pull the ST card and say whatever, it works in this instance? Just be cautious about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T11:13:52-08:00","id":326164,"title":"","content":"A Demon wouldn't get skills out of a Pact, but if they incorporated the musical background into their Cover (IE spent the Cover experience) then they could use Legend to fake it. There's a variety of embeds that could also help: Download Knowledge, Like I Built It (for playing an instrument), Clothes Make the Man, and/or Persistent Legend come to mind. I wouldn't be surprised if there are other embeds that could apply as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}